# Great Train Heist, first mode: the additional combat phase is only "if it's your combat phase" (CR 500.8), the untap works on any turn. Bot1's Memnite attacked on turn 3 and is still tapped
# on turn 4. Bot2's Memnite attacks, Bot1 casts the untap mode in Bot2's declare attackers step, and the untapped Memnite blocks it: both die, and play goes on to Bot2's second main phase (no extra combat).

[Bot1 Deck]
Memnite
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Mountain
Great Train Heist
Island
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T4 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
Bot2.Attack(Memnite > Bot1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Great Train Heist.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Untap all creatures)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Tapped = false
Bot1.Block(Memnite > Memnite)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Step = Main2
Bot1.Graveyard = Memnite; Great Train Heist
Bot2.Graveyard = Memnite
